  {"clause_id": "c001",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Recipient\" is defined collectively as both Dr. June personally and the Trustees of the University of Pennsylvania, leaving it uncertain whether each obligation binds the individual, the institution, or both jointly. The phrase \"materials developed at St. Jude\" is also broader than the item later defined in section 1.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.10}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c002",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.07},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.06}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Materials\" is defined to include \"any progeny, portions, unmodified derivatives and any accompanying know-how or data,\" and the boundary of \"unmodified derivatives\" and \"progeny\" is not fixed; whether a lentiviral vector clone incorporating the construct falls inside the definition is contestable. The undefined \"accompanying know-how or data\" is equally open-ended.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.42},
     {"issue": "The definition covers only \"unmodified derivatives,\" but section 7 indemnity speaks of \"the Materials and their progeny or derivatives\" without the qualifier, so the two provisions describe different subject matter.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.26}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c004",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.13},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c005",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The carve-out \"Except as provided in this Agreement\" does not identify what licence, if any, the Agreement does grant, so the scope of the permission implied by the section 3 purpose clause is left to inference. The reach of \"other proprietary rights\" against the enumerated patents, applications and trade secrets is also open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.18}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c006",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.14},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c007",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The \"sole purpose\" grant is drawn in technical terms — production of a molecular lentiviral vector clone \"in quantities sufficient to complete a Phase I clinical trial\" — and whether particular downstream uses (further trials, manufacture, collaboration) fall inside that single permitted purpose is genuinely contestable. \"Quantities sufficient\" and \"the Recipient's clinical facilities\" both lack a fixed boundary.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.48},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.20}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c008",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Another institution\" is undefined and it is unclear whether it captures a commercial company, a collaborating hospital, or an affiliate of the Recipient, and whether \"taken or sent\" reaches products made from the Materials rather than the Materials themselves.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.32},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.13}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c009",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Provided to a commercial entity\" and \"research that is subject to consulting or licensing obligations to another party\" are both undefined, so whether a sponsored collaboration or a licence of Recipient's own inventions trips the restriction is contestable. The parenthetical carve-out for U.S. government grantee obligations sharpens the expressio unius question about other pre-existing obligations.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.44},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.16}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c010",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.15},
     {"issue": "Section 4 requires only that a copy of a publication be provided (naturally read as after publication), while the last sentence of section 5 forbids publication without 30 days' prior submission for review; the two publication regimes must be reconciled.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.36}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c011",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.16},
     {"issue": "The flat acknowledgment of St. Jude ownership of the Materials \"and any progeny thereof\" sits awkwardly with the same section's statement that \"Ownership shall [follow] inventorship according to US patent law\" and with the contact-to-determine-ownership sentence, which assume ownership is yet to be worked out.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c012",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The trigger \"which could not have been produced but for the use of the Materials\" is an open-ended causal test, and the obligation itself — to \"contact St. Jude to determine ownership interests, if any\" — states no standard, outcome or consequence. What compliance looks like is therefore indeterminate.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.41},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.20}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c013",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The one-line rule \"Ownership shall [follow] inventorship according to US patent law\" is garbled and does not say whether it governs only the patent applications described in the preceding sentence or ownership of the Materials generally. Its interaction with the flat ownership acknowledgment in the same section is left unresolved.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.38},
     {"issue": "It cannot readily be squared with the first sentence of section 5, in which Recipient acknowledges St. Jude's ownership of the Materials and any progeny regardless of who invents.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.31}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c014",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"The results of such research\" has no clear antecedent: it may mean all research using the Materials, or only research yielding a patent application or commercial product as described in the immediately preceding sentences. The scope of the pre-publication review duty turns entirely on that word \"such.\"", "type": 1, "prob": 0.72},
     {"issue": "It is in tension with section 4, which contemplates simply supplying St. Jude a copy of any publication containing results obtained from use of the Materials, with no prior-review condition.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.44}
   ]}
]}

